  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">JPO [Japan] for Culture and Emergencies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Junior Professional Officer (JPO) position operates under the authority of the Assistant Director-General for Culture, with supervision from the Director of the Entity and relevant Chief of the units. The JPO&apos;s responsibilities include conducting research, compiling analyses, and participating in studies or publications. They ensure that knowledge management systems related to program implementation are up-to-date and shared with staff across locations. Additionally, the JPO assists in program activities, prepares for meetings and events, manages administrative and financial procedures, and contributes to progress reports. Participation in official events, preparation of correspondence and reports, and the maintenance of digital institutional memory are also part of the role.</narrative>
  </description>
